Title: Gap B: write UNINSTALL.md as the R15 removal procedure
Created: 2026-09-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-03T16:47Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0613 (goal 1 of the ladder), gap B. `Ticket-ref: tickets/0613`
— this ticket does not close the tracker; gap C remains blocked elsewhere.

`R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state` is `not-offered` for zoteus. The
2026-09-03 ruling (0613's log) retired the earlier reading that zoteus must
grow a callable uninstall verb: an external MCP server has no host uninstall
lifecycle to hook, so the ratified surface for this architecture class is a
**published removal procedure** the harness can execute verbatim and sweep.
Two preconditions the ruling attached: TMPDIR/XDG redirection in the arena
(status not re-checked here — 0613's log said only HOME was redirected as of
2026-09-03), and a dedicated account owning the arena rather than the
operator's home — **that second precondition is done**: ticket 0625 closed.

Form is already decided (0613's log, 2026-09-03T13:43Z): not an upstream
issue asking the maintainer to write this — **we draft it ourselves**, in
this project's own documentation voice (`docs/configuration.md`,
`docs/semantic-search.md`), using the declared derived-state roots from
`bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s Declaration (data dir, model cache
under it since upstream PR #27) phrased as steps a user follows, with the
pre-PR-#27 case as the worked example of why "just delete the data
directory" was wrong before that merge.

**Per this repo's own upstream discipline**: a repo-side PR is the spec/
measurement record, not the shipped artifact — the actual upstream
submission is a separate, GOVERNANCE.md-gated action, not something this
ticket files on its own. This ticket's deliverable is the drafted procedure,
committed in this repo, ready for that later hand-off.

## Actions

1. Read `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s Declaration for the exact
   derived-state roots (data dir path, model cache location relative to it).
2. Draft `UNINSTALL.md` in this project's own docs style, listing concrete
   removal steps (exact paths, in the order a user would follow them).
3. Include the pre-PR-#27 case as a worked example (why "delete the data
   directory alone" was wrong before the model cache moved under it).
4. Note in the draft, or in this ticket's log, whether TMPDIR/XDG redirection
   in the arena is confirmed complete — if not, flag it rather than silently
   assuming the ruling's other precondition is satisfied.
5. Do NOT open an upstream PR from this ticket. Commit the draft in this
   repo and reference the GOVERNANCE.md lane that owns the hand-off.

## Test

- The draft's removal steps are checked against the adapter's own Declaration
  programmatically where possible (e.g. a test asserting every path the draft
  names appears in the Declaration, and vice versa) rather than eyeballed —
  the exact class of drift PR #27 exists to prevent from recurring silently.

## Verification

- [ ] `UNINSTALL.md` drafted, paths sourced from the Declaration, not guessed
- [ ] Pre-#27 worked example included
- [ ] TMPDIR/XDG redirection status recorded (confirmed or flagged open)
- [ ] No upstream PR opened by this ticket

## Invariants

- The dedicated-account precondition (0625) is not touched or re-verified
  here — it's independently closed.
- Gap C stays out of scope; this ticket does not touch R22.

## Exit criteria

- `UNINSTALL.md` is drafted and committed, its removal steps traceable to the
  adapter's Declaration, and 0613's log records the draft plus the
  TMPDIR/XDG redirection finding.
